Package: DRBayes
Type: Package
Title: Bayesian Doubly Robust Causal Inference Methods
Version: 0.1.0
Author: Tomotaka Momozaki <t_momozaki@rs.tus.ac.jp>
Maintainer: Tomotaka Momozaki <t_momozaki@rs.tus.ac.jp>
Description: Implements Bayesian doubly robust methods for causal inference, 
    including posterior coupling and Bayesian bootstrap approaches. 
    Provides tools for simulation studies and synthetic data generation.
    The package includes functions for generating synthetic datasets,
    running parallel simulations, and estimating average treatment effects
    using state-of-the-art Bayesian methods. 
    When using this package, please cite: Orihara, S., Momozaki, T., 
    & Sugasawa, S. (2025). Bayesian Doubly Robust Causal Inference via 
    Posterior Coupling. arXiv preprint arXiv:2506.04868.
